{
  "character": "国",
  "summary": {
    "text": "国, “country,” is a simplified form of 國. The outer enclosure remains, while the inner 或 has been replaced by 玉. Remembering the modern shape as “jade within borders” may help, but the older character has a different explanation: an enclosure supplies meaning and 或 supplies sound.",
    "evidence_ids": [
      "E1",
      "E3",
      "E4",
      "E9",
      "E11"
    ]
  },
  "history": [
    {
      "text": "For 國, the phonetic analysis in Dong Chinese and Wiktionary connects 囗, an enclosure, with 或 as a pronunciation cue. The Shuowen also records the pairing of 囗 and 或. These are accounts of 國; the 玉 inside 国 belongs to the simplified form and should not be projected back into that older structure.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "E3",
        "E9",
        "E10",
        "E11"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "uncertainties": [],
